## Fix: nulhomotopy_R2_from_unbounded_component boundary conditions

### Problem
Admits 2 and 3 in nulhomotopy_R2_from_unbounded_component (the boundary
conditions F(x,0)=g(x) and F(x,1)=k(x) for the translation homotopy F)
were previously coded with a `set F_trans := graph ...` abbreviation.
The `rewrite (apply_fun_graph ...)` tactic failed because Megalodon's
rewrite pattern matching doesn't transparently unfold local `set` definitions
containing other local `set` definitions (r2sub) to match the LHS pattern.

### Fix
1. Replaced `set F_trans := graph ...; witness F_trans` with
   direct `witness graph (setprod A unit_interval) (fun q => r2sub ...)`.
   This puts the explicit graph term in the goal so apply_fun_graph matches.

2. Used `claim Happly0 : ... { exact (apply_fun_graph ...) }; rewrite Happly0`
   pattern instead of `rewrite (apply_fun_graph ...)` directly.
   The claim+exact approach works because Megalodon uses definitional equality
   for `exact` (beta-reduction of the graph application), while `rewrite`
   requires syntactic pattern matching.

### Status
- nulhomotopy_R2_from_unbounded_component: 2 admits remain (F continuity,
  scaling homotopy H). F boundary conditions now fully proved.
